---
import PageLayout from '../layouts/PageLayout.astro';
import { CONTACT_EMAIL } from '../site';
---

<PageLayout
  title="Privacy policy"
  description="What data pulse360 collects, how cookies and analytics are used, and your choices."
  updated="October 16, 2026"
>
  <p>
    This policy explains what information is collected when you visit pulse360.news
    and how it is used. We keep data collection to a minimum.
  </p>

  <h2>Information we don't collect</h2>
  <p>
    pulse360 has no accounts, sign-ups or comment forms. We don't ask for your name,
    email address or any other personal details to read the site.
  </p>

  <h2>Stored on your device</h2>
  <p>
    Your theme preference (light or dark) and any articles you bookmark are saved in
    your browser's local storage. That data stays on your device and is never sent to
    us. The site also uses a service worker to cache pages so they load faster and work
    offline. You can clear both at any time in your browser settings.
  </p>

  <h2>Analytics</h2>
  <p>
    We use Google Analytics to understand how the site is used: which pages are read,
    roughly where visitors come from and what devices they use. Google Analytics uses
    cookies and collects information such as your IP address, browser type and the
    pages you visit. We use this only in aggregate, to improve the site. Learn more
    about <a href="https://policies.google.com/technologies/partner-sites" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">how Google uses data from sites that use its services</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>Advertising</h2>
  <p>
    pulse360 may display ads served by Google and its partners. Third-party vendors,
    including Google, use cookies to serve ads based on your previous visits to this
    and other websites. Google's use of advertising cookies enables it and its partners
    to serve ads to you based on your visits to this site and/or other sites on the
    internet.
  </p>
  <p>
    You can opt out of personalized advertising in
    <a href="https://adssettings.google.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Google Ads Settings</a>,
    or opt out of other vendors' use of cookies for personalized advertising at
    <a href="https://www.aboutads.info/choices/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">aboutads.info</a>.
    When ads are shown to visitors in the European Economic Area, the UK and
    Switzerland, a consent message asks for permission before personalized ads or
    non-essential cookies are used.
  </p>

  <h2>Links to other websites</h2>
  <p>
    Our briefs link to the original reporting on other websites. Those sites have
    their own privacy policies, and we aren't responsible for their practices.
  </p>

  <h2>Children</h2>
  <p>pulse360 is a general news site and isn't directed at children under 13.</p>

  <h2>Your rights</h2>
  <p>
    Depending on where you live, you may have rights to access, correct or delete
    personal data held about you. Because we hold no personal data ourselves, most
    requests concern Google's services, which you can manage through your Google
    account and the links above. For anything else, contact us.
  </p>

  <h2>Changes and contact</h2>
  <p>
    If this policy changes, we will update it here and change the date above.
    Questions: <a href={`mailto:${CONTACT_EMAIL}`}>{CONTACT_EMAIL}</a>.
  </p>
</PageLayout>
